1309-5.2.10 INTRQ (Device interrupt)
1310-
1311-This signal is used to interrupt the host system. INTRQ is asserted only when the device has a pending
1312-interrupt, the device is selected, and the host has cleared the nIEN bit in the Device Control register. If the
1313:nIEN bit is equal to one, or the device is not selected, this output is in a high impedance state, regardless of
1314-the presence or absence of a pending interrupt.
1315-
1316-The interrupt pending condition shall be cleared by:
1317-   - assertion of RESET-; or
1318-   - the setting of the SRST bit of the Device Control register; or
1319-   - the host writing the Command register; or
1320-   - the host reading the Status register.
