1351-
1352-This signal is negated to extend the host transfer cycle of any host register access (Read or Write) when the
1353-device is not ready to respond to a data transfer request.
1354-
1355-If actively asserted, this signal shall only be enabled during DIOR-/DIOW- cycles to the selected device. If
1356:open collector, when IORDY is not negated, it shall be in the high-impedance (undriven) state.
1357-
1358-The use of IORDY is required for PIO modes 3 and above.
