1893-7.3.1 Power modes
1894-
1895-The lowest power consumption when the device is powered on occurs in Sleep Mode. When in Sleep Mode,
1896-the device requires a reset to be activated. The time to respond could be as long as 30 seconds.
1897-
1898-In Standby Mode, the device interface is capable of accepting commands, but as the media may not be
--
1942-In the Active, Idle, and Standby modes, the device shall have DRDY bit of the Status register set and, if BSY
1943-bit is not set, shall be ready to accept any command.
1944-
1945-In Sleep mode, the device's interface is not active. A host shall not attempt to read the device's status or
1946-issue commands to the device.
