2399-7.10 DOOR LOCK (removable)
2400-
2401-OPCODE - DEh
2402-TYPE - Optional
2403-PROTOCOL - Non-data command.
2404-INPUTS - None.
--
2412-DESCRIPTION - This command either locks the device or media, or provides the status of the media change
2413-request button.
2414-If the device is not locked, the device shall be set to the locked state and good status returned.
2415-If the device is locked, the status returned shall indicate the state of the media change request button. Good
2416-status shall be returned while the media change request button is not active, and the MCR bit in the Error
2417-register and the ERR bit in the Status register shall be returned when the media change request button is
2418-active.
2419:When a device is in a DOOR LOCKED state, the device shall not respond to the media change request
2420-button, except by setting the MCR status, until the DOOR LOCKED condition is cleared. A DOOR LOCK
2421-condition shall be cleared by a DOOR UNLOCK or MEDIA EJECT command, or by a hardware device reset.
2422-
