4425-8.7 Device 0 only configurations
4426-
4427-In a single device configuration where device 0 is the only device and the host selects device 1, device 0
4428:may respond to accesses of the Command Block and Control Block registers in one of two methods. These
4429-two methods exist because previous versions of the ASCI X3T10 standard did not specify the required
4430-behavior for this configuration. The first method is the recommended implementation.
4431-
4432-The first method is:
4433-     a) A write to the Device Control register shall complete as if device 0 was the selected device;
4434-     b) A write to the Command Block register, other than the Command register, shall complete as if device
4435-     0 was selected;
4436-     c) A write to the Command register is ignored;
4437:     d) A read of the Control Block or Command Block registers, other than the Status or Alternate Status
4438-     registers, shall complete as if device 0 was selected;
4439-     e) A read of the Status or Alternate status register returns the value 00H.
4440-     NOTE 41 - IDX is vendor specific and might change following reset or power mode changes resulting
4441-     in other values for status other than 00H.
4442-
4443-The second method requires that device 0 implement an Error, Status and Alternate Status register that is
4444-used whenever device 1 is selected.
--
4448-     NOTE 42 - IDX is vendor specific and might change following reset or power mode changes resulting
4449-     in other values for status other than 00H.
4450-     b) A write to the Device Control register shall complete as if device 0 was the selected device;
4451-     c) A write to the Command Block register, other than the Command register, shall complete as if device
4452-     0 was selected;
4453-
4454-70
4455:                                                                                                               X3T10/0948D Revision 4c
4456-
4457-     d) A write to the Command register with a command code other than the INITIALIZE DEVICE
4458-     PARAMETERS or EXECUTE DEVICE DIAGNOSTICS command causes the device 1 Error, Status and
4459-     Alternate status registers to be used as follows:
4460-
4461-          1) the BSY bit is set in the device 1 status register;
4462-          2) the ABRT bit is set in the device 1 Error register;
4463-          3) the ERR bit is set in the device 1 status registers;
4464-          4) the BSY bit is cleared in the device 1 status register;
4465-          5) if the nIEN bit in the Device Control Register is cleared, the INTRQ signal is asserted;
4466-          e) An EXECUTE DEVICE DIAGNOSTIC command is executed as if it addressed to device 0;
4467-     f) An INITIALIZE DEVICE PARAMETERS command is executed as if device 1 is present and is actually
4468-     executing the command. The command shall have no effect of the device parameters of device 0;
4469:     g) A read of the Control Block or Command Block registers, other than the Status or Alternate Status
4470-     registers, shall complete as if device 0 was selected;
4471-     h) A read of the Error, Status or Alternate status register returns the value in the device 1 copy of these
4472-     registers. The device 1 status registers shall contain 00H following a reset and the value 01H following
4473-     an attempt to execute a command, other than EXECUTE DEVICE DIAGNOSTICS or INITIALIZE
4474-     DEVICE PARAMETERS, on device 1.
