5485:C.3.3 CS1- (Device chip Select 1)
5486-
5487:Hosts shall provide CS1- on both the pins identified in table C.1.
5488:Devices are required to recognize only one of the two pins as CS1-.
5489-
5490-C.3.4 DMACK- (DMA Acknowledge)
5491-
5492-This signal is optional for hosts and devices.
5493-If this signal is supported by the host or the device, the function of DMARQ shall also be supported.
5494-
5495-C.3.5 DMARQ (DMA Request)
--
5510-C.3.8 SELATA- (Select 68-pin ATA)
5511-
5512-This pin is used by the host to select which mode to use, PC Card-ATA mode or the 68-pin ATA mode. To
5513-select 68-pin ATA mode, the host shall assert SELATA- prior to applying power to the connector, and shall
5514-hold SELATA- asserted.
5515-The device shall not re-sample SELATA- as a result of either a Hard or Soft Reset. The device shall ignore
5516-all interface signals for 19 ms after the host supplies Vcc within the device's voltage tolerance. If SELATA- is
5517:negated following this time, the device shall either configure itself for PC Card-ATA mode or not respond to
5518-further inputs from the host.
5519-C.4 Removability considerations
5520-
5521-88
5522:                                                                                                               X3T10/0948D Revision 4c
5523-
5524-This standard supports the removability of devices that use the ATA protocol. As removability is a new
5525-consideration for ATA devices, several issues need to be considered with regard to the insertion or removal
5526-of devices.
5527-
5528-C.4.1 Device recommendations
5529-
5530-The following are recommendations to device implementors:
5531:          - CS0-, CS1-, RESET- and SELATA- should be negated on the device to prevent false selection
5532-          during hot insertion.
5533-          - Ignore all interface signals except SELATA- until 19 ms after the host supplies VCC within the
5534-          device's voltage tolerance. This time is necessary to de-bounce the device's power on reset
5535-          sequence. Once in the 68-pin ATA mode, if SELATA- is ever negated following the 19 ms de-bounce
5536-          delay time, the device should disable itself until VCC is removed.
5537-          - The DOOR LOCK and DOOR UNLOCK commands and the MC and MCR bits in the Error register
5538-          should be used to prevent unexpected removal of the device or media.
--
5547-          address is inserted or removed.
5548-          - The removal or insertion of a device at the same address should be detected so as to prevent the
5549-          corruption of a command.
5550-          - The DOOR LOCK and DOOR UNLOCK commands and the MC and MCR bits in the Error register
5551-          should be used to prevent unexpected removal of the device or media.
5552-
5553-                                                                                                                                              89
5554:X3T10/0948D Revision 4c
5555-
5556-                                                      Annex D.
5557-
5558-                                                                (informative)
5559-
5560-                          Identify device data for ATA devices below 8 GB
5561-
--
5589-
5590-For drives less than or equal to 528 MB, Identify Data word 1 (Default Cylinders) shall not specify a value
5591-greater than 1,024.
5592-If a drive is greater than 528 MB but less than or equal to 8 GB, the maximum value that shall be placed into
5593-this word is determined by the value in Word 3 as shown in the following table.
5594-
5595-90
5596:                                                                                        X3T10/0948D Revision 4c
5597-
5598-                                              Value in Word 3  Maximum value in Word 1
5599-                                                     1 1h      65,535 FFFFh
5600-                                                     2 2h      65,535 FFFFh
5601-                                                     3 3h      65,535 FFFFh
5602-                                                     4 4h      65,535 FFFFh
5603-                                                     5 5h      32,767 7FFFh
--
5644-accessed in the current translation mode. If an Initialize Drive Parameters command has not been executed,
5645-the contents of this word shall be the same as word 1. If an Initialize Drive Parameters command has been
5646-executed, this word is the integer result of dividing the total number of user sectors (this value may be in
5647-words 60-61) by the number of sectors per logical cylinder ( [word55] x [word56] ), but shall not be a value
5648-greater than 65,535.
5649-
5650-                                                                                                               91
5651:X3T10/0948D Revision 4c
5652-
5653-D.2.7 Word 55
5654-
5655-Identify Data word 55 (Current Heads) is the number of heads specified by the last Initialize Drive
5656-Parameters command. This word may contain a value of between 1 and 16. If an Initialize Drive
5657-Parameters command has not been executed, the contents of this word shall be the same as word 3.
5658-
--
5683-addressing mode.
5684-The values in words 1, 3, and 6 should be selected such that the number of orphan sectors is minimized.
5685-Normally, the number of orphan sectors should not exceed ( [word55] multi [word56] - 1 ). However, the host
5686-system can create conditions where there are a larger number of orphans sectors by issuing the Initialize
5687-Drive Parameters command with values other than the values in words 3 and 6.
