  4427: In a single device configuration where device 0 is the only device and the host selects device 1, device 0
  4428: may respond to accesses of the Command Block and Control Block registers in one of two methods. These
  4429: two methods exist because previous versions of the ASCI X3T10 standard did not specify the required
  4430: behavior for this configuration. The first method is the recommended implementation.
  4431: 
  4432: The first method is:
  4433:      a) A write to the Device Control register shall complete as if device 0 was the selected device;
  4434:      b) A write to the Command Block register, other than the Command register, shall complete as if device
